WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.773
Gravitational-wave inference usually assumes
detector noise is Gaussian and stationary,

00:00:05.853 --> 00:00:07.185
but real LIGO, Virgo,

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:11.760
and KAGRA data break that with glitches and
drifting spectral lines.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.267
This work introduces SLIC, Score-based Likelihood
Characterization.

00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:22.657
It learns the true noise distribution with a
diffusion model and couples it to a differentiable

00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:25.550
waveform for unbiased parameter estimation.
